      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1373826872,
      "text": "Agave colorata, the mezcal cenizo, is a species of flowering plant in the family Asparagaceae. It is native to Sonora and southwestern Sinaloa in Mexico. A succulent reaching 1 to 1.5 m, it is typically found on rocky outcrops in desert or dry scrubland at elevations from 50 to 500 m. It has been assessed as Least Concern. Valued as an ornamental for its blue-grey leaves, it is available from commercial suppliers."
    }
